{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And now, go (lekhah) and I will send you to Pharaoh.</b> It should have said 'and now, go' (לך); and by way of the plain sense (peshat) the added הֵא (heh) alludes to the five days that they would encamp at Mount Sinai — that is, from the new moon of Sivan until the sixth day, on which they received the Torah. Therefore it says, 'and this shall be the sign for you' — the sign of the added הֵא, whose numerical value is five; and it says, 'when you bring the people out of Egypt, you shall serve Elohim on this mountain' — five days, and on the sixth you will receive the Torah." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah,</b> the added heh in the word לכה is the final heh of the Name; therefore it says, 'and this shall be the sign for you,' for the sign of the heh is called 'this' (זה), in the manner of (Exodus 15) 'זה אלי ואנוהו' — 'this is my El and I will glorify Him'; 'בעבור זה עשה HaShem לי' — 'because of this HaShem did for me.' Therefore it says, 'כי אהיה עמך' — 'for I will be with you' — and behold, the sign of the covenant is that He will be with him, and you have no sign greater than this; and it is fitting that all should believe."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:48.948010139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}